 :context
 "Ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (capable model + mandatory verification per
  agent) after a prior 18-agent haiku batch had a 61% defect rate. 30+ consecutive
  agents on this stricter protocol had succeeded before this one. Built from
  cloud-itonami-isic-0122 (growing of tropical and subtropical fruits) as the
  module-structure template, with clojure -M:test independently re-run from fresh
  clones before and after push. The kotoba-lang/industry registry entry for \"0127\"
  was independently re-verified (fresh clone) before any implementation work to
  confirm id/name match: {:id \"0127\" :name \"Growing of beverage crops\" ...} --
  no mismatch (multiple prior agents in this fleet had mislabeled their assigned
  ISIC class). `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0127` returned 404
  before work began, confirming a fresh from-scratch scaffold."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct field-equipment operation (grower's exclusive authority)"
  "finalizing a spray-application decision (agronomist/grower authority)"
  "harvest-timing / replanting economic decisions (remain human authority)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0127 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0122 module-for-module,
  namespace beverageops.*):
  - Governor (BeverageOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks
    (plantation-not-registered, no-execution, field-equipment-or-spray-blocked,
    op-not-allowed, plantation-count-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate
    crop-health concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (seedling/fertilizer/equipment),
    beverage-crop classes (coffee/tea/cacao/yerba-mate)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    plantation-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-plantation lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0122's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main, verified end-to-end
  - Operations: log-plantation-record, schedule-field-operation,
    flag-crop-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 30 tests / 92 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green (1 fewer assertion than 0122's 93 because facts covers 4 beverage-crop
    classes vs 0122's 5 fruit classes)
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Beverage-crop-growing (0127) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (field-equipment operation, spray-application finalization)
    hardcoded in governor checks, not just asserted in prose"
   "Crop-health escalation (flag-crop-health-concern always human) is a core
    design invariant"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0122's own stub status"]}

